      "id": "s1q1",
      "number": 1,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Add the polynomials. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (3x^2 + 5x - 2) + (x^2 - 3x + 7) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q1_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "4x^2 + 2x + 5",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Combine like terms: group the x² terms, the x terms, and the constants separately.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (3x^2 + x^2) + (5x - 3x) + (-2 + 7) = 4x^2 + 2x + 5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q2",
      "number": 2,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Add the polynomials. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (2x^3 - x + 4) + (x^3 + 3x^2 + 2x - 1) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q2_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "3x^3 + 3x^2 + x + 3",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Line up like terms: x³, x², x, and constants. Remember 2x³ + x³ = 3x³.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (2x^3 + x^3) + (3x^2) + (-x + 2x) + (4 - 1) = 3x^3 + 3x^2 + x + 3 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q3",
      "number": 3,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Subtract the polynomials. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (5x^2 - 3x + 1) - (2x^2 + x - 4) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q3_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "3x^2 - 4x + 5",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute the negative sign first: -(2x² + x - 4) = -2x² - x + 4. Then combine like terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 5x^2 - 3x + 1 - 2x^2 - x + 4 = 3x^2 - 4x + 5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q4",
      "number": 4,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Subtract the polynomials. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (4x^3 + 2x^2 - x + 6) - (x^3 - 3x^2 + 5x - 2) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q4_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "3x^3 + 5x^2 - 6x + 8",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute the negative to every term in the second polynomial, then combine like terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 4x^3 + 2x^2 - x + 6 - x^3 + 3x^2 - 5x + 2 = 3x^3 + 5x^2 - 6x + 8 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q5",
      "number": 5,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Simplify. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (3x^3 - 2x^2 + x) + (x^3 + 4x^2 - 5) - (2x^3 - x^2 + 3x - 1) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q5_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "2x^3 + 3x^2 - 2x - 4",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Handle one operation at a time. Add the first two, then subtract the third. Distribute the negative carefully.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 3x^3 - 2x^2 + x + x^3 + 4x^2 - 5 - 2x^3 + x^2 - 3x + 1 \\)<br>\\( = (3+1-2)x^3 + (-2+4+1)x^2 + (1-3)x + (-5+1) = 2x^3 + 3x^2 - 2x - 4 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q6",
      "number": 6,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( 3x(2x^2 - 5x + 4) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q6_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "6x^3 - 15x^2 + 12x",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute 3x to each term: 3x · 2x² = 6x³, 3x · (-5x) = -15x², 3x · 4 = 12x.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 3x(2x^2) + 3x(-5x) + 3x(4) = 6x^3 - 15x^2 + 12x \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q7",
      "number": 7,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply using FOIL. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (x + 4)(x - 3) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q7_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "x^2 + x - 12",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "FOIL: First (x·x), Outer (x·(-3)), Inner (4·x), Last (4·(-3)).",
      "solution_html": "\\( x^2 - 3x + 4x - 12 = x^2 + x - 12 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q8",
      "number": 8,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply using FOIL. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (2x - 5)(x + 3) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q8_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "2x^2 + x - 15",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "FOIL: F = 2x·x = 2x², O = 2x·3 = 6x, I = -5·x = -5x, L = -5·3 = -15.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 2x^2 + 6x - 5x - 15 = 2x^2 + x - 15 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q9",
      "number": 9,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply using FOIL or the box method. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (3x - 2)(4x + 1) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q9_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "12x^2 - 5x - 2",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "F = 3x·4x = 12x², O = 3x·1 = 3x, I = -2·4x = -8x, L = -2·1 = -2. Combine the middle terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 12x^2 + 3x - 8x - 2 = 12x^2 - 5x - 2 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q10",
      "number": 10,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (x + 2)(x^2 - 3x + 5) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q10_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "x^3 - x^2 - x + 10",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute x across (x² - 3x + 5), then distribute 2 across (x² - 3x + 5). Combine like terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( x^3 - 3x^2 + 5x + 2x^2 - 6x + 10 = x^3 + (-3+2)x^2 + (5-6)x + 10 = x^3 - x^2 - x + 10 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q11",
      "number": 11,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (2x - 3)(x^2 + 4x - 1) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q11_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "2x^3 + 5x^2 - 14x + 3",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute 2x and then -3 across the trinomial. You get 6 partial products — combine the x² terms and the x terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( 2x^3 + 8x^2 - 2x - 3x^2 - 12x + 3 = 2x^3 + (8-3)x^2 + (-2-12)x + 3 = 2x^3 + 5x^2 - 14x + 3 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q12",
      "number": 12,
      "section": "B",
      "standard": "S1.b",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Multiply. Write your answer in standard form.<br>\\( (x^2 - 2x + 3)(x^2 + x - 4) \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q12_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "x^4 - x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 12",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Use the box method (3x2 grid). Write one polynomial across the top, one down the side, fill each cell, then combine diagonals.",
      "solution_html": "\\( x^4 + x^3 - 4x^2 - 2x^3 - 2x^2 + 8x + 3x^2 + 3x - 12 \\)<br>\\( = x^4 + (1-2)x^3 + (-4-2+3)x^2 + (8+3)x - 12 = x^4 - x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 12 \\)"
    }
  ]
